# Folders Vulture skips by default, in .vultureignore syntax.
#
# A scanned project brings one back with a negation in its root
# .vultureignore: `!build/` scans every directory named `build`, `!web/build/`
# that one only. A .gitignore cannot bring one back. Version-control stores
# (.git, .svn, .hg, .bzr) and Python virtualenvs (a directory holding
# pyvenv.cfg) are skipped by the scanner itself and are never brought back.
#
# Each line is one directory-name glob ending in `/`, matching a directory of
# that name at any depth: no `!`, and no `/` inside the name.
#
# Edit this file, at the repository root. The scanner, the backend and the
# opengrep plugin are each built from their own directory, so each carries a
# byte-identical copy that its tests compare with this one. After an edit:
#   for d in agents/shared/shared/tools backend/pkg/scanignore plugins/opengrep/src; do cp default.vultureignore "$d/"; done

